  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  Kernel-checked Lean 4 results around the Riemann Hypothesis, which remains open. Unconditional:
  0 <= Lambda <= 0.2811857 for the de Bruijn-Newman constant (Newman's conjecture along Dobner's proof, also for
  the extended Selberg class; the upper bound from OpenAI's and Liu's zero-free half-planes via de Bruijn's
  theorem), and pole-free Weil positivity on the window of half-width 0.5493. Conditional or equivalences:
  RH is equivalent to Weil positivity on pole-free tests and to that positivity outside the window, and a
  family of Riemann-Roch-square windows covering every pole-free test would imply RH; no such family is
  constructed. Packaged with the three papers and a vendored copy of the Telperion certificate engine.
